          %title
          %h1#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a collection of “parameterized objects”, i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+elements"} generalized elements
            of the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in the image of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            and and with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
            read as “ordinary element of a set” is yields the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of the (co)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
          %p
            Moreover, the description of of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of a presheaf in terms of a pullback of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            generalizes directly to categories of generalized elements.
          %h1#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            equipped with a choice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi pt
                    %mi D
                  %mo :
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_D : {*} \to D
            of one of its objects.
          %p
            Recall that a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi pt
                    %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_D \to d
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            may be called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            “with domain of definition” being the object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_D
          %p
            For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            the canonical choice is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi pt
                    %mi Set
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_{Set} = {*}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            set with a single element. Generalized elements of a set “with domain of definition”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*}
            are just the ordinary elements of a set.
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ({pt_D/D})
            is the category of generalized elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            with domain of definition
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_D
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                objects are such generalized elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi pt
                        %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta : pt_D \to d
                of objects
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
            %li
              %p
                morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo →
                      %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \to \gamma
                are given whenever a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi d
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : d \to d'
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                takes the element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta'
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi pt
                                %mi D
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi δ
                              %mo ↙
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mrow
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mo ′
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi d
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi d
                              %mo ′
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; pt_D
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}^\delta\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\delta'}
                      \\\
                      d &amp;&amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp;&amp; d'
                      }
                      \\,.
          %p
            Notice that the canonical projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi pt
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (pt_D/D) \to D
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
            that forgets the tip of these trangles may be regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            for the given pointed category
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi pt
                            %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (pt_D/D) &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  D^I &amp;\stackrel{d_0}{\to}&amp; D
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{d_1}
                  \\\
                  D
                  }
          %p
            (see also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
            for more on this perspective). So in fact such “categories of generalized elements” are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundles"} generalized universal bundles
            in the 1-categorical context. And both are really fundamentally to be thought of as intermediate steps in the computation of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limit"} weak pullbacks
          %p
            The above allows to generalize the notion of
            %em category of generalized elements
            a bit further to that of generalized elements of functors with values in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
            be a functor with codomain our category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            with point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_D
          %p
            The
            %strong category of generalized elements
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi El
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi pt
                        %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi pt
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El_{pt_D}(F) := C \times_D (pt_D/D)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi El
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi pt
                                %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi pt
                            %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  El_{pt_D}(F) &amp;\to&amp; (pt_D/D)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  C &amp;\stackrel{F}{\to}&amp; D
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p This means:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi El
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi pt
                            %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El_{pt_D}(F)
                are all the generalized elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi pt
                        %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_c : pt_D \to F(c)
                for all
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
            %li
              %p
                a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_c \to \delta_{c'}
                between two such generalized elements is a commuting triangle
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi pt
                                %mi D
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mi c
                              %mo ↙
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi c
                                      %mo ′
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi F
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi c
                              %mo ′
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; pt_D
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}^{\delta_c}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\delta_{c'}}
                      \\\
                      F(c) &amp;&amp; \stackrel{F(f)}{\to} &amp;&amp; F(c')
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                for all morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : c \to c'
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h1#examples Examples
          %h2#ordinary_category_of_elements ordinary category of elements
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi pt
                    %mi Set
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_{Set} = {*}
            the above reproduces the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
          %h2#action_groupoid Action Groupoid
          %p
            Given a vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo •
                  %mo ⟲
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\bullet\righttoleftarrow G
          %p
            is canonically identified with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Vect
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{B} G \to Vect
                  \\,.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : ({*} \stackrel{g}{\to} {*}) \mapsto
                  (V \stackrel{\rho(g)}{\to} V)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            of
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            has a standard point
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mi Vect
                    %mo →
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pt_{Vect} \to Vect
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            itself, regarded as the canonical 1-dimensional
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
            of generalized elements of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi pt
                    %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (pt_{Vect}/ Vect)
            has as objects pointed vector spaces and as morphisms linear maps of pointed vector spaces that map the chosen vectors to each other.
          %p
            Now, as described in detail at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            the category of generalized elements of the representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V//G
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acting on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Vect
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Vect
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  V//G &amp;\to&amp; Vect_*
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B} G &amp;\to&amp; Vect
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            As described there,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V//G \to \mathbf{B}G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            incarnation of the vector bundle that is associated via
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            to the universal
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/06/an_exercise_in_groupoidificati.html#c017574"} Exploding a Category
